    "specPath": "specs/020-local-development-builds/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "The route from this checkout to a running Butler on the developer's own Mac, which no spec claimed: a `make dev` hot-reload loop and a `make app` that produces an ad-hoc signed `Butler.app` and installs it. It needs no Developer ID, no notarization and no repository secret, because nothing it produces is published: the artifact carries no authority in its signature and says so. Spec 017 is untouched and still governs anything a stranger downloads. The costs an ad-hoc signature imposes, chiefly that macOS re-asks for Screen Recording after every rebuild, are written down rather than papered over.\n",
    "title": "Local development builds: run and install Butler on your own machine without a signing identity"
  },
